<title>MOROCCO: Morocco cuts May domestic oil product prices.</title>
<headline>Morocco cuts May domestic oil product prices.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco's monthly industrial fuel oil price has been set at 1,662.9 dirhams ($175) per tonne for May, down 65.29 dirhams on the previous month, Morocco's energy ministry said.</p>
<p>Gas oil and kerosene fell respectively 16 and nine cents to 4.86 dirhams and 3.24 dirhams a litre, the ministry said.</p>
<p>It attributed the reductions to a fall in prices on the international market.</p>
<p>Pump prices of super and ordinary petrol remained unchanged at 7.65 dirhams and 7.42 dirhams a litre respectively.</p>
<p>($1 = 9.5 dirhams)</p>
</text>
